      "summary": "The log processor can leave sensitive text in the body exported for records without structured properties or scopes. The AC-05 capture test checks FormattedMessage and attributes, so it does not detect this path.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 113,
          "message": "Unstructured log bodies can bypass AC-05 redaction because the processor leaves LogRecord.Body intact while clearing only FormattedMessage.",
          "confidence": 0.89,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "When a log has no structured data, RedactingLogProcessor clears FormattedMessage and Attributes but leaves LogRecord.Body unchanged. The configured log exporter can export the body; CaptureLogs in DiagnosticsTests snapshots FormattedMessage and Attributes only.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs an interpolated message containing a credential or prompt with no properties or scopes. The processor clears FormattedMessage but leaves the canary in Body, so the exporter can still send it; the AC-05 test does not inspect Body and can pass. OWASP A04:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
