      "summary": "The configured logging pipeline can still export sensitive text from LogRecord.Body when a record has no structured properties or scopes. The regression test does not inspect Body.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 111,
          "message": "The no-properties path leaves LogRecord.Body intact, allowing interpolated sensitive text to reach the exporter despite clearing FormattedMessage.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "In the no-structured-data branch, the processor clears FormattedMessage and Attributes but leaves LogRecord.Body unchanged. The exporter receives the record after this processor.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs request-derived text with an interpolated message and no properties or scopes, such as `logger.LogError(exception, $\"Authorization: {token}\")`. The processor clears FormattedMessage but retains the interpolated text in Body, so the exporter can send the token to Application Insights. The test snapshots only FormattedMessage and Attributes, so it would not catch this leak. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
